1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Vernon Edward Svarverud'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was September 9 for Vernon Edward Svarverud of Eugene, who died September 4 of Liver failure, he was 64. 
2 CONT Svarverud was born August 7, 1936, in Eugene to Clarence and Ethel McCubins Svarverud. He grew up in central Oregon in Terrebonne and Culver, and graduated in 1964 from Culver high School. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He served four years in the Navy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Svarverud married Paralyn Harper in Eugene on September 11, 1959. He worked 38 years at Georgia Pacific Corp.
2 CONT
2 CONT His interests included hunting and fishing, and he was a firearm enthusiast.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife; two sons, Mark and Marlin, both of Eugene; and a sister, Carolyn Stallings of Redmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be from 4 p.m. to 8 p.m. Friday at Chapel of memories Funeral Home in Eugene. Saturday's service will be at 2 p.m., also at the funeral home. Burial will be at Lane Memorial gardens, Eugene. Memorial contributions 
2 CONC may be made to the Cowboy Church of Oregon, in care of Tom Crabb.
